      <span class="eyebrow">Rotterdam permits</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="permit-title">Permit process in Rotterdam</h2>
      <p>The Rotterdam Omgevingsvergunning process for facade signage involves three checks: structural (is the attachment safe?), aesthetic (does the signage fit the streetscape and the building?), and environmental (does the illumination level meet local standards?). For heritage buildings or signage on a prominent location, the welstandscommissie reviews the aesthetic submission in detail.</p>
      <p>Our role: we prepare the full technical dossier (dimensioned drawings, material specification, illumination calculation, mounting detail), submit it to the municipality on your behalf via the Omgevingsloket portal, respond to any queries during the review, and schedule installation immediately after permit grant. Typical lead time is four to eight weeks for the permit, two to three weeks for production in parallel. For non-permitted signage (small printed boards inside the threshold, internal signage, fully reversible heritage-friendly installations) we skip the permit step and deliver within two weeks.</p>
